            <ArticleTitle>Spindle Cell Sarcoma of the Iliac Vein on 18 F-FDG PET/CT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-294</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RLU.0000000000001548</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 44-year-old woman with a protruding mass of the right thigh underwent an F-FDG PET/CT and gadolinium-enhanced MRI. The F-FDG PET/CT scan revealed mildly increased F-FDG uptake in a large mass involving the right common and external iliac veins. The gadolinium-enhanced MRI revealed a well-enhancing soft tissue mass inside the right common and external iliac veins. The mass was diagnosed as high-grade spindle cell sarcoma with fibroblastic differentiation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
